Couple of scripts here.

mkfileset:

	Creates a fileset (currently in a filesystem called NOC) hanging off the
    root of the filesystem. 
	The clever bit (if there is one) is that it fudges mmedquota to allow you
    to set a fileset  quota without going into vi
	
	Syntax is mkfileset filesetname size(GB) path description"

	Where: path is the subpath for the fileset - ie for /NOC/TEST path would
    be TEST.


gpfsdf:
	lists all filesets on a filesystem (currently hard coded to NOC) together
    with their quotas and useage.
	Requires Python 3 (it was ported from Python 2). It now exits non-zero if
    mmrepquota or mmlsfileset fails, rather than printing an empty table.
	A manual page is available: man -l ../../man/gpfsdf.1

Note: mkfileset and mmsetfsquota are tcsh scripts and reference a site-specific
path for the nocmmsetquota helper (adjust the EDITOR path inside them for your
deployment).
